  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper fits long-term (Δt ≈ 504 trading days) logarithmic return distributions for 31 financial assets using a discrete-time quantum walk model with four parameters (η, θ, φ, ω) optimized via hill climbing. Using n = 100 time steps (and a smoothed ensemble with n ~ N(100, 15²)), the model achieves mean absolute errors on the order of 0.5–1.2 × 10^-2 and KS statistics roughly 0.045–0.341, generally outperforming Gaussian fits for asymmetric distributions.",
